<p>Hungarian authorities have opened an espionage case against investigative journalist Szabolcs Panyi, accusing him of spying for Ukraine as campaigning heats up before next month’s election. Panyi rejected the claim as false and unjust. The New York Times described the case as part of Prime Minister Viktor Orban’s intensifying campaign against critics ahead of a tough April vote.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/Sx9pWWnoT5HX1iZEJlhEruNIUb4b58cqLtyuuGp2ifoP4__3fkkOsgX2yUMKkKgaIHdx97fAxYyadI4qhZq8sL-Ds1y6NfI0MkJPmyUkl8uRAWWx-diNaXHbLrAjx0MWZVRxcTsWkzrJfzzkr68-f-dfdDvlMZ6kD6jgoqByriIZGznOJOO_GraOcrFEpUUm' alt='The investigative journalist Szabolcs Panyi in Budapest in 2021. He dismissed the government’s espionage claims as a “false” and “completely unjust accusation.”' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Moscow backdrop: The Guardian reported that the case emerged as Orban’s government dealt with fallout from allegations that Hungary’s foreign minister had shared confidential EU information with Sergei Lavrov.</li><li>EU strain: The Guardian said the affair capped a week in which Hungary’s relations with the EU sank to new lows.</li><li>Quiet raid resurfaced: RT said a July 8, 2025, operation involving opposition-linked IT staff drew little attention at the time and became public only this week.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Hungarian government: Authorities said they had opened an investigation into a journalist over accusations that he was spying for Ukraine during an increasingly bitter election campaign. (<a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/hungary-government-accuses-journalist-of-spying-for-ukraine'>The Straits Times</a>)</li><li>Szabolcs Panyi: The journalist rejected the espionage allegation, calling it a false and unjust accusation. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/26/world/europe/hungary-journalist-election-meddling-espionage.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>RT&#x27;s account of Hungarian security services: RT cast the affair as part of a wider struggle involving alleged Ukrainian-linked operatives, a secret-service raid, and suspected efforts to influence Hungarian politics through opposition-linked figures. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/636295-hungary-ukraine-election-spies/'>RT</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/636295-hungary-ukraine-election-spies/'>Battle for Hungary: The Ukraine connection</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/26/hungary-charges-journalist-szabolcs-panyi-following-claims-minister-was-in-touch-with-moscow'>Hungary charges journalist after claims minister was in touch with Moscow</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/26/world/europe/hungary-journalist-election-meddling-espionage.html'>Hungary Opens Espionage Case Against Journalist</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/europe/hungary-government-accuses-journalist-of-spying-for-ukraine'>Hungary government accuses journalist of spying for Ukraine</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>